# Screenshots that contain live credentials in plaintext.
#
# These were captured while setting up Supabase and Netlify, and they show a
# database password and a personal access token as readable text. Rotating both
# is the real fix; until then these must not be pushed anywhere, because a
# commit is permanent and a leaked token outlives the repo it leaked from.
#
# Paths here are relative to THIS directory (drive/), not to the repo root.
# The same rule is mirrored in the repo-root .gitignore as a second lock.
docs/setup-screenshots/*SECRET*.png
docs/setup-screenshots/_token-*.png